Not quite. You need {noi} and {zi'e} to connect descriptors that way:

{la daraiavauc noi nolraitru banli zi'e noi nolraitru le nolraitru zi'e noi
nolraitru le gugde zi'e noi bersa la victaspa'as zi'e noi me la xaxamanic
zi'e noi pu zbasu ti noi nolzda}

Lojban words can't start with {'}, but they can start with {x}; lojban
words tend to avoid the schwa except where necessary for word construction,
so either dropping the "h" or repeating the starting vowel or using a {x}
is probably preferable to starting with a schwa.

You shouldn't make it a fu'ivla (IMHO) because it has limited utility; you
can make something called a "stage-2 fu'ivla", which is really just a
glorified name, by taking the name and prepending {me} to it (e.g. {me la
xaxamanic}, which means "one of the ones referred to by the name
'xaxamanic'").

